+# Why CVE-2007-3477 Is Already Fixed in libwmf 0.2.12 on Debian Bookworm
+
+---
+
+## CVE-2007-3477 – Already Fixed (Tracker Bookkeeping Issue)
+
+**Component:** `gdImageFilledArc()` in `src/extra/gd/gd.c` (bundled GD library inside libwmf)
+**Issue:** CPU consumption DoS via large start/end angle degree values passed to arc drawing functions
+**Impact:** Denial of service (CPU exhaustion) — no code execution, no data exposure
+**CVE filed against:** libgd before 2.0.35 (2007); also affects libwmf's bundled GD copy
+
+---
+
+## Vulnerability Overview
+
+* **Component impacted:** `gdImageFilledArc()` and `gdImageArc()` in libwmf's internal bundled copy of GD (`src/extra/gd/gd.c`)
+* **Nature of issue:** When large angle values are passed, the original loop:
+
+  ```c
+  while (e < s) {
+      e += 360;
+  }
+  ```
+
+  can run indefinitely, consuming 100% CPU
+* **Severity:** Low (CVSS v2: 4.0 — network, no auth required, availability impact only)
+* **Attack vector:** Remote authenticated — crafted WMF/input triggering arc rendering
+* **CVE originally filed against:** libgd before 2.0.35 (released 2007)
+
+---
+
+## libwmf 0.2.12 (Debian Bookworm) – Already Fixed
+
+* **Upstream fix commit:** `cfc09169386c00052b03703e115d8c9e0e4a7883` (short: `cfc0916`)
+
+* **Fix commit date:** 2018-08-08 — explicitly labeled "CVE-2007-3477" by upstream maintainer Caolán McNamara
+
+* **Release date:** v0.2.12 released on 2019-02-01 (fix predates release by ~6 months)
+
+* **Fix inclusion:** Commit `cfc0916` is an ancestor of v0.2.12
+
+* **Nature of fix:**
+
+  * Replaces infinite loop logic
+  * Introduces modulo-360 normalization
+  * Adds bounds checking for negative values
+  * Handles edge cases safely
+
+* **Debian Bookworm version:** `libwmf 0.2.12-5.1` (includes fix)
+
+* **Tracker discrepancy:**
+
+  * Debian Security Tracker marks bookworm as "vulnerable"
+  * This is a **bookkeeping issue**
+  * Fix was included silently in upstream release (not a dedicated security release)
+  * Tracker was never updated accordingly
+
+---
+
+## Why No Patch Is Needed
+
+* The fix is already present in `src/extra/gd/gd.c` in libwmf 0.2.12
+
+* Vulnerable loop:
+
+  ```c
+  while (e < s) { e += 360; }
+  ```
+
+  has been removed
+
+* Fixed implementation includes:
+
+  ```c
+  if (s > 360) { s = s % 360; }
+  if (e > 360) { e = e % 360; }
+  ```
+
+  along with proper validation and normalization
+
+* **libgd2 (standalone)** is also fixed in Debian Bookworm (`2.3.3-9`)
+
+* No major vendor issued a libwmf-specific advisory:
+
+  * Red Hat: WONTFIX (2008)
+  * Ubuntu: Low priority / ignored
+  * SUSE: Fixed only standalone GD (2007)
+
+* Debian tracker status (`unimportant + vulnerable`) is stale and does not reflect actual code state
+
